WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.690
In the Bible, a man called
Job suffers terribly,

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.030
though he has done nothing wrong.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.590
He loses his wealth, his
children and his health,

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.730
and he wants to know why.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.160
Christians face the same
puzzle today, after floods,

6
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.230
earthquakes and disease.

7
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.850
Most do not deny the problem at all.

8
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.390
So what answers do Christians
give when disaster strikes,

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.870
and do any of them really work?

10
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.270
In this mission, you'll compare two
famous attempts to explain evil,

11
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.160
from Saint Augustine and from John Hick.

12
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.340
Then you'll put each answer to
the test, one case at a time.

13
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.520
Your mission: find out what answers
Christians give to suffering,

14
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.650
and weigh up whether any of them work.
